   "sentenceId": 3,
   "he": "וּמִצְטָרְפִין זֶה עִם זֶה. תָּנָא: הַתְּבוּאָה וְהַקְּמָחִים וְהַבְּצֵיקוֹת מִצְטָרְפִין זֶה עִם זֶה. לְמַאי הִלְכְתָא?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that each one of the five types of grain «joins together with the others» to constitute the measure that obligates one to separate ḥalla. It was «taught» in a baraita: With regard to grain from «produce and flours and pieces of dough,» each one of these «joins together with the others.» The Gemara asks: «With regard to what halakha» was this taught?"
  }
